ple lost their jobs during  this time and  do unemployment rates and lack of money  coming in does that  play a role in the lack of divorces i  mean i'm not going to  beat around the bush divorce is  expensive it's expensive to begin with  and then we add this factor of  unemployment and  how are we going to deal with the  settlement that would come in i mean you  don't really know what's going on with  the business  and sometimes it's a family business on  top of it so finances aren't just the  basic finances of divorce but really  what that settlement and  what the entire family would look like  with these new restrictions in place as  well  so it could really just be a pause in  divorce because of the finances  associated with this  is it basically one of those situations  where time will tell  as soon as this pandemic is over i have  to be completely transparent mercedes  time will absolutely  well we appreciate your knowledge and  great  information lacey thank you so much las  vegas now we'll be right back
 

